ertime artifact.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 65 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent French Hill (R) is running."]}, "overview": "French Hill, the Republican incumbent, seeks another term in a central Arkansas district that leaned Republican by eight points at the last presidential election. He enters the final stretch with a major financial advantage, having raised about $5.0 million to Chris Jones's $1.8 million, and with most national raters calling the race Likely Republican; two outlets rate it Lean Republican.\n\nJones, a first-time candidate, has kept the race competitive. The only independent poll of the fall, from Hendrix College in August, showed him ahead by four points, and the broader environment favors Democrats. Republican groups have spent the closing weeks attacking Jones over financial disclosure complaints, while outside money has flowed into the district. Markets price Hill as a clear favorite, but the race appears closer than the district's partisan baseline alone would suggest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1835, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3532, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3233, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2423, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2933, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3205, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3445, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2683, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2648, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2693, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2035, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2922, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2948, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1951, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "20